#!/usr/bin/env bash
#
# deploy-5.18.105.sh — on Uganda, no phone number in any log line: the log statements that could carry a customer's or a
# staff member's number masked, PluginLog::tail() for the three that keep two digits, and the report's BY NUMBER column
# padded by characters — plugin 5.18.105, Uganda; root docs/74, 9 Nov — over 5.18.104 (live), every switch of the sales
# follow-up kept exactly as found; or roll it back to 5.18.104, every switch still kept.
#
#   5.18.105 No phone number in a log line (Uganda; root docs/74 §A, §H.1): the owner's rulings of 8 and 9 Nov — option
#            B, every log line that can carry a number on Uganda. 21 runtime files change, 35 masked log lines among
#            them (LN-01…LN-35, 37 statements): where the line already names its record, the number goes; where it named
#            nothing else, a record id takes its place; the webhook log's three phone fields keep •••• and the last two
#            digits (PluginLog::tail()). The report's BY NUMBER table pads by characters, not bytes. Nothing else changes:
#            no message, send, screen or stored record; no new setting; NO MIGRATION. The sales follow-up's ladder is
#            5.18.104's, byte for byte (its tool, its two classes, master, the event processor, NotificationService and
#            089–091 held by their sha256), and THIS SCRIPT KEEPS EVERY ONE OF ITS KEYS AS FOUND: it never runs the switch
#            tool's on, off, skip, set or erase, nor scripts/sales-followup.sh, before, during or after the copy, or in
#            the rollback — the steps that are on when it runs (on 13 Nov: 1 report, 2 ack and 3 tracking; 4–6 follow
#            in the ladder's order) keep running through the deploy, and are judged, never required off. Step 12 (offers-live)
#            waits until 5.18.105 serves and its --after-only has passed. South Sudan: the lines it shares with Uganda
#            lose their numbers too, nothing else changes. Files, against 994d660: 45 changed, 43 added — 88
#            (the added ones are its tests).
#
#   THE FIGURES GO TO A CASH SHEET, NEVER TO THE TERMINAL OR THE LOG. Each run writes its own sheet,
#            /root/dnb-5.18.105/cash-<mode>-<UTC stamp>.txt, mode 0600, in a folder of mode 700. It holds the book's cash in
#            hand before and after, the parts, P0's own output, the tool's, the drift and its row ids, and the lines of
#            the physical count; for ECO Bank, each offered account's row id, its last kept line's date and whether a
#            statement is kept; the copy checks' and N1's counts; the quoting checks' counts and uCRM client ids — the
#            app's clients filed under another organization (Q-N2) and the two Q-CA3 probed; and the catalogue's items
#            (QL-G1, QL-N7) — each plan's and kit's row id and name, and the installation's, with its uCRM link record and
#            the uCRM product (and service plan) it names by id, its unit and the resolver's reason, which can carry a
#            price; per item, under "uCRM items with the same spelling — a hint only", the uCRM items spelled like it, by
#            id and name, each with whether it could be linked or the rule that stops it; the organization numbers uCRM
#            gives its products; what the forms would offer from uCRM in direct mode (QC-G1, QC-CA1) — each plan pair's
#            and hardware item's uCRM ids, name, price and unit, the installation's, every other item with its reason —
#            the uCRM catalogue's settings on the copy by record id, uCRM id and name, the waiting web applications' ids
#            (QC-N4) and, after a rollback, the web-direct applications with no quotation made, by id (QC-RB2: a record
#            only, nothing for the rollback to quote by hand — 5.18.103, put back, handles each exactly as it did before
#            5.18.104, docs/72 G-10, §G.8). The terminal and the log carry its path, its line
#            count and the first 16 hex of its sha256, and `less <path>` — counts, hashes, organization ids, role names
#            and PASS/FAIL/NOTE, never a figure, a price, a product's, a person's or a customer's name, phone, amount or
#            account number, a staff id, or an account's name, number or ending — so the log can be sent and the
#            terminal pasted. The row ids the log carries are G3's ("account #<id>", an offered bank account's row in the
#            chart of accounts), uCRM's organization ids and the id of one uCRM client attribute (QL-N1); the one kind
#            of name it prints is an ORGANIZATION's, one line per organization uCRM lists (Q-G4): DishNet's own
#            companies, printed on every quote — never a client's. The catalogue checks (QL) print fixed category
#            counts, read states and HTTP codes, and besides them only the salesPerson attribute's id (QL-N1),
#            quotation 000314's item types with whether each carries a productId and a unit (QL-N2), set or unset and
#            on or off for three settings (QL-N6), and two dates, the newest plan save and the newest kit (QL-N5); the
#            uCRM catalogue checks (QC) counts by the release's why codes, read states and HTTP codes; the owner checks
#            (TN) counts and role names only; the sign-off checks (QS) counts of lines of code only. Read
#            the sheet on the server; never paste it, copy it or send it.
#
#   ON COPIES, NEVER ON THE LIVE BOOK. Every reading of the book here is of a consistent copy: VACUUM INTO, as the database's
#            owner, exactly as the backup makes its copy, into a folder of mode 700 in the container's /tmp; beside it,
#            copies of the three configuration files and of the vault holding only the book's own keys (tenant_profile,
#            currency_code, currency_symbol, cashbook_base_currency, cashbook_currencies) and ECO Bank's switch
#            (bank_screen_enabled) — never webhook_secret_file, never a credential. The quoting checks' copies hold the
#            same keys and the two organization keys (ucrm_quote_organization_id, ucrm_lead_organization_id), from the
#            files, the vault and the store row — and, as the one exception 5.18.99's SPEC §6 states (Q-G4b),
#            crm_auth_token and crm_base_url alone, from the store row, in a file of mode 0600 in a folder of mode 700,
#            deleted by the probe once read and by this script after it, never printed; the catalogue checks (QL) use
#            that same token copy for their token client. The catalogue checks run this release's UcrmQuoteLines and
#            UcrmQuoteLinks — the PIN's before the copy (its lib/UcrmQuoteLinks.php required into the local reading by that
#            file's own path, never the live root's copy — the same file at 5.18.102, 5.18.103 and the pin), the INSTALLED
#            ones after it, where no link is read (UcrmQuoteLinks only empty, under offered(); QL-CA1 and QL-LK1 retired
#            since 5.18.103, QC-CA1 instead) — on such a copy, with
#            a vault of their own: the link store read on the copy only (UcrmQuoteLinks::fromStore, whose load() would
#            create the table in a live store), its records judged by the remote reading through
#            UcrmQuoteLinks::fromRecords, and the resolver constructed directly on clients built here: never
#            UcrmQuoteLines::quoteClient(), which returns a client nothing wraps, and never forPage(), which writes its
#            page cache (ucrm_quote_catalogue_cache.json) into the data folder it is given. 5.18.103's checks (QC) read the
#            same way: the RELEASE's lib/UcrmCatalogue.php required by its own path (the pin's before the copy, the
#            installed after it), its records read on the copy only (UcrmCatalogue::fromStore, which never creates the
#            table), and UcrmQuoteLines::offered() on the clients built here over UcrmCatalogue::fromRecords — never
#            forDirectPage(), which writes the page cache and the last good copy into its data folder, nor
#            forDirectUse(), whose quoteClient() returns a client nothing wraps. The owner checks (TN-G2,
#            TN-CA2, RB) read the staff rows and the channel registry
#            on such a copy, its settings row cut to the book's keys, through each code root's own SalesNumbersAdmin — no
#            Evolution client is ever constructed; wa_inbox_roles alone is read from the live store row, read-only
#            (TN-G3, TN-CA3). The sign-off checks (QS) read webhook.php as text — the pin's from Git, the installed file in
#            place — and run none of it. Each code root reads its own copy (the constructor alters tables and applies a
#            migration, PluginConfig::load refreshes the vault it is given) and is itself a copy, in the container's /tmp
#            — never the plugin folder, whose parent holds the live vault. Every PHP process the cash, bank, copy,
#            quoting, catalogue and owner checks run on a copy has its own DN_VAULT_FILE. The live vault's sha256 and time
#            are read before and after every batch of runs on copies, and again at the end (Z1); nothing of the vault, no
#            webhook_secret and no token copy is left under the run's folders in /tmp (Z2). Every copy is removed at once,
#            and again when the run ends. No page or CSV is rendered with a login on the live install.
#
#   UCRM IS READ WITH GETS ONLY (5.18.99's SPEC §6, carried). Every uCRM client the quoting and catalogue checks hold —
#            the plugin's own (CrmApiClient::fromUcrm, the live ucrm.json read in place) and, when crm_auth_token is set,
#            the token client built exactly as KycService::postQuote builds it — is wrapped: get() is passed on and
#            counted; post, patch, put, delete and anything else are counted and refused before they reach the client.
#            The catalogue's clients get the shorter limits 5.18.102's CrmApiClient offers (withTimeouts(5, 30), set on
#            the client before it is wrapped); through the resolver each reads exactly GET products?limit=500, then GET
#            service-plans?limit=500, and nothing else — the check QL-G1 makes, and QC-G1 and QC-CA1 through offered() —
#            and, after QL-G1's, the script's own
#            raw GET of each of those two lists once more, for the organization field uCRM gives its rows (a note at
#            QL-G1), counted on its own, every one a GET; quotation 000314 is read back once (GET billing/quotes/{id}, by
#            the quote id its application stores; QL-N2), and the salesPerson attribute through the release's own lookup
#            (QL-N1). The run's count of other requests must be 0 (Q-G4, Q-CA3, QL-G1, QC-G1, QC-CA1). Nothing is ever
#            created, changed or deleted in
#            uCRM — no quote, no client, no product, no attribute. No key is ever set: ucrm_quote_organization_id and
#            wa_inbox_roles included.
#
#   5.18.105'S OWN CHECKS (root docs/74 §H.4, §H.5): THE LADDER KEPT AS FOUND (LK). LK-G1, stage A: the ladder's keys —
#            SalesFollowupLadder::allKeys() and settingKeys() — read read-only in four places (<data>/kyc_config.json,
#            its store row, <plugin>/data/config.json, <data>/config.json): NO-GO only where a place cannot be read, or an
#            allKeys() key is held by a config.json (the tool's off would read back FAIL key_outside_overrides); never
#            for a key that is on — a note gives the steps on and skipped, the ledger, the counts per place, every key
#            where file and store disagree; A NOTE IN CAPITALS when offers_live_enabled is set. LK-B1, after DEPLOY and
#            before the copy: the same reading, equal key by key and place by place, or NO-GO and nothing is copied
#            ("the switch tool was run meanwhile"). LK-CA1 after the copy: equal to LK-B1's (FAIL otherwise); LK-CA2:
#            no table's rows fell (quote_followup_state over its rows not list_last:%), _schema_checks unchanged, the
#            four jobs' schedule entries kept; LK-ON: each step on, the installed tool's --check against the pin's at
#            stage A (PASS then FAIL now is a FAIL); LK-AO in --after-only, against the deploy's map, a note. Each key's
#            value is a 16-hex HMAC under a key kept in /root/dnb-5.18.105/lk-key-5.18.105 (mode 0600) — the map on the
#            sheet and in the state file, never a value in the log. THE MASKED LINES (LM). LM-G1, stage A: in the pin's
#            files from Git each of the build's blocks (one per hunk, from Git, markers aside; counted as blocks of
#            lines by sha256 — this script carries no source text) once and its old block nowhere, the control on
#            994d660; LM-G2: the on-chase precondition's two strings once each in the pin's evo_webhook.php; LM-CA1 the
#            same on the installed files; LM-CA2 the PHP log's old-form opt-out lines 60 s or more after the copy (0,
#            else FAIL) and the sinks' records with a run of 9 or more digits since then (a note); LM-ON in
#            --after-only; LM-RB1 after a rollback: the old blocks back. THE ROLLBACK (RB105): LK-RB0 before ROLLBACK is
#            typed; after the put-back master and the four jobs, LK-RB1 (every key in every place, the tool's show and
#            the rows as before), the open quote follow-ups and running offers counted, LM-RB1.
#
#   5.18.104'S CHECKS, CARRIED AND MADE LIVE-AWARE (root docs/74 §H.4.4). The paragraphs below are 5.18.104's, and
#            stand as amended here: QF-G1 accepts only 5.18.104's tables as it left them (088 last is "open the
#            plugin once"); QF-G2, VN-G7 and OF-G2 only "none pending"; QF-G4 is retired (LK-G1), with
#            --clear-switches, which is refused; QF-CA2's and QF-CA3's dark-build judgements are LK-CA2's; QF-CA3 lists
#            each job OFF (switch) exactly when its flag is unset; QF-CA5, VN-CA1 and OF-CA1 equal stage A's readings
#            through the pin's code; VN-CA2's ai_media as its flag says; VN-CA4's keys are LK-CA1's, its rows a note;
#            OF-CA3's late counts a note; AC-CA1's on() as its key says. RETIRED with the off-all rollback: QF-RB1–QF-RB3,
#            VN-RB1–VN-RB4 and VN-RB6, OF-RB1, AC-RB1; VN-RB5, OF-RB2 and AC-RB2 are notes ("they continue under 994d660
#            as their switches say").
#
#   5.18.104'S OWN CHECKS, Part F's (QF, "follow-up"; root docs/73 §H.2.15): counts, fixed codes and key names only in
#            the log, the report's owners on the sheet. Refusals before the copy, each on a copy of the book through the
#            PIN's code from Git: QF-G1 the copy's shape — 088 last and none of 089–091 (a first deploy), or all three
#            applied (a redeploy after its rollback); anything else NO-GO; QF-G2 the one migration trial for every part
#            (ruling R10) — 089 → 090 → 091 through the pin's MigrationRunner, each _schema_checks row at its count (on a
#            first deploy each applied and its migration.log line OK; on a redeploy none pending, the rows already there
#            the verdict and the live log's lines a note), the pin's doctor PASS for all three, and Part V's negative
#            control (an 085-shaped wa_media: PARTIAL, no row); QF-G3 the pin's record-only hooks, each counted in its
#            method (NotificationService's in sendVia, sendDocument and sendImage), W1–W3 and NOTIFY_KINDS' events, as
#            text, and HK7, the pin's send-site inventory, by its own scan and class table on its own tree;
#            QF-G4 the one rule for every part's keys (ruling R7) — every key of SalesFollowupLadder::allKeys() unset in
#            the live files and the store row: a key set is NO-GO unless, on a redeploy, --clear-switches is given; a key
#            held by data/config.json or <data>/config.json is NO-GO always. Notes: QF-N1–QF-N7 (the stored values and
#            dn_tz(), the enquiry follow-ups, the pin's report as the baseline, the Message Log's sends per handset and
#            Kampala day against the daily cap,
#            the master log against reminder_hour, the PHP log, the daily list's size). After the copy, on fresh copies
#            through the INSTALLED code: QF-CA1 089–091 applied at the first boot; QF-CA2 and QF-CA3 what the dark build
#            could have written — no ledger row and no run of the four jobs after the copy (judged in the deploy run; on
#            a redeploy against the baseline taken just before the copy; the schedule read, with other jobs' entries in
#            it, the control); QF-CA3 the four jobs registered and listed OFF (switch); QF-CA4 the F1 filters, with an
#            enquiry row returned as the control; QF-CA5 the tool's show — all thirteen steps off, the ledger off — and
#            "not this install" as South Sudan; QF-CA6 the gates off, and as South Sudan, beside the control (every key
#            on Uganda: true, one mark); QF-CA7 a note; QF-CA8 the recorders with their controls — each reading of a
#            copy with the copy's own vault. In an --after-only run, QF-ON0–QF-ON5 through the installed tool's --check
#            on a copy (L-ON through the installed ladder where `skip ack` left the ledger on and step 2 off; QF-ON3's
#            spacing as Q3-ON judges it), each judging only a step that is on. After ROLLBACK is typed, before the
#            put-back: QF-RB1; then QF-RB2 (a note)
#            and, after the put-back, QF-RB3 (the rollback paragraph below).
#
#   5.18.104'S OWN CHECKS, Part V's (VN "voice notes", VA "voice acknowledgement"; root docs/73 §H.3.25): counts,
#            fixed codes and key and schema names in the log; event ids, the baseline's largest ids and the first OpenAI
#            call's date on the sheet; the OpenAI key "set" or "not set", never its value; nothing calls OpenAI. Refusals
#            before the copy, on a copy through the PIN's code and as the pin's text from Git: VN-G1 a read of QF-G4's
#            one rule for Part V's keys (its settings printed, never NO-GO); VN-G2 none of 090's tables on a first
#            deploy, exactly 090's objects and its _schema_checks row on a redeploy; VN-G4 the pin's voice gates as text
#            (8c inside its try/catch, every gate call passing the data directory, the fromMe branch 5.18.103's but
#            for W1, the OpenAI key's input empty on Uganda, ruling R1's ai_media line, 090 against 089, no INDEXED BY);
#            VN-G6 no voice event on a first deploy (on a redeploy, the history counted); VN-G7 090's half of QF-G2's
#            trial. Notes: VN-G3 the key set or not, ai_provider, ai_enabled; VN-G5 the voice baseline. On a redeploy
#            VN-G6 takes VN-CA4's baseline in QF-G1's own call, at its one moment. After the copy: VN-M1 and VN-M2 090
#            on the book; VN-CA1 the installed gates off on Uganda and inert as South Sudan with every voice key on;
#            VN-CA2 ai_media listed OFF (switch) by cron_status, and never as South Sudan; VN-CA3 the event
#            processor's two lists; VN-CA4 nothing of Part V written by the dark build (judged in the deploy run);
#            VN-K1 the key in none of the plugin's logs; VN-K2 the installed tab. In an --after-only run, VA-ON1 and
#            VN-ON1–VN-ON4 through the installed tool's --check, each step that is on. In the rollback, VN-RB1–VN-RB4
#            read QF-RB1's result before the put-back; after it, VN-RB5 and VN-RB6 (an instruction to rotate the key
#            whenever OpenAI was called).
#
#   5.18.104'S OWN CHECKS, Part O's (OF, "offers"; root docs/73 §H.4.18): counts, fixed codes, key and schema names and
#            handset labels in the log; offer ids, the baseline's largest ids and the copy's start on the sheet. NOTHING IS
#            EVER SENT and no request reaches Evolution: every OF reading runs with PHP's network functions off. Refusals
#            before the copy, on QF-G2's trial copy through the PIN's code: OF-G1 a read of QF-G4's one rule for Part O's
#            keys (ruling R7; it clears nothing itself), no wa_offer* table on a first deploy, and on a redeploy said in
#            capitals with the offers not closed counted by state (their ids on the sheet); OF-G2 Part O's share of
#            QF-G2's one trial (ruling R10) — 091 ok, never partial, its _schema_checks row 25 of 25, OfferSchema::check()
#            empty, and every existing table's rows unchanged, by count and by a hash of every row. Notes: OF-N1 the
#            baseline audience through the pin's store-free OfferAudience::build() on that copy (on a first deploy the
#            reasons that need 089–091 objects read "not measured before 089"); OF-N2 R-01's lines in the PHP log over 30
#            days; OF-N3 the settings offers read, Part O's keys as stored and the staff without a phone. On a redeploy
#            OF-CA3's baseline is taken in QF-G1's own call, at its one moment. After the copy: OF-M1 091 on the book (its
#            md5, its row, OfferSchema); OF-M2 its migration.log line; OF-CA1 screen() and live() off, the menu entry
#            once inside OfferSwitch::screen(, the tab's "not switched on" card as an admin, beside two controls; OF-CA2
#            ruling R1's four lines in master, offers_send once and last; OF-CA3 nothing of Part O written by the dark build
#            (judged in the deploy run; on a redeploy against its baseline, each act by what its maker could know, ruling
#            R18); OF-CA4 South Sudan with both offer keys on: live() off, the job — included on a scratch folder with no
#            book — writes nothing and loads no sender, the tool "not this install"; OF-CA5 OfferSwitch::declaredKeys()
#            inside the ladder's keys. In an --after-only run, OF-ON1 and OF-ON2 through the installed tool's --check
#            offers-test and offers-live, each step that is on. In the rollback, OF-RB1 reads QF-RB1's result before the
#            put-back (Part O's hook before its keys, the offers paused, claimed recipients settled uncertain or returned
#            to queued, ruling R12; no offer running, no recipient claimed); after it, OF-RB2 (a note).
#
#   5.18.104'S OWN CHECKS, Part P's (AC, "agent copy"; root docs/73 §H.5.14): counts and fixed codes in the log; never
#            an address, a quote number or an account's id. NOTHING ASKS uCRM — plugin mail is judged from
#            email_settings.json — and NO E-MAIL LEAVES THE CONTAINER. Refusal before the copy: AC-L1 the server's own
#            PHP lints the pin's lib/QuoteAgentCopy.php and the three files P7 changes (P7S-07). P7's keys are QF-G4's
#            (ruling R7): P7 has no stage-A rule of its own. Notes, on a copy through the PIN's code: AC-N1 how plugin
#            mail is configured, the two quotation paths, email_cc_contacts, kyc_quote_send_via_crm, automatic quoting
#            and the accounts by kind (accountCounts(), counts only); AC-N2 what the copy would have covered over 30
#            days, by path, an upper bound. After the copy, through the INSTALLED code: AC-CA1 QuoteAgentCopy::on()
#            off on the live configuration's copy, on with the key set (the control), off with it set as South Sudan,
#            and P7's two collections absent on a first deploy (counted, never read, otherwise); AC-CA2 the positive and
#            negative controls on a copy of the book, made unable to reach a live system first and read back so
#            through the installed MailService (P7S-02: a fresh email_settings.json on the pin's loopback relay, no
#            ucrm.json in reach, no WhatsApp sender, fixture accounts under example.test only), uCRM the pin's recording
#            fake — the app and the webhook paths copied, the customer's own address and a quote with no record not,
#            and with the key unset, or set as South Sudan, every e-mail equal to 5.18.103's. In an --after-only run,
#            AC-ON1 through the installed tool's --check agent-cc, while agent-cc is on. In the rollback, AC-RB1 reads
#            QF-RB1's result before the put-back (Part P's two keys cleared last, with the record keys, no hook, read
#            back off, quote_agent_cc_admins as it was; ruling R11); after it, AC-RB2 (a note: both collections stay).
#
#   5.18.103'S CHECKS, CARRIED (QC, "quote catalogue"), their ids kept so that none reads as another release's, counts and
#            fixed why codes only in the log (root docs/72 §G.13). The switch is as an admin last left it on the uCRM
#            catalogue screen (turned on in production on 4 Nov 2026, under 5.18.103; root docs/07), and the copy changes
#            nothing of it: every count of what is offered is a note. Refusal before
#            the copy: QC-G1 what the forms would offer in direct mode — through the PIN's UcrmQuoteLines::offered() over
#            the copy's catalogue settings (the pin's UcrmCatalogue by its own path), through the plugin's own client and,
#            when crm_auth_token is set, the token client, GET-only: NO-GOs that no flag lifts — an unreadable catalogue
#            (either client); an answer whose why code is outside the release's set, or whose reason is empty ("other");
#            a request but the two lists; the settings on the copy unread, or the pin without lib/UcrmCatalogue.php; the
#            items' keyed hashes not made. With no quoting organization in force (Q-G3) QC-G1 is a note: the catalogue lives
#            under the gate. Notes, counts only: QC-G1's items not offered, by why; QC-N1 the switch as stored — a note
#            either way, never in capitals: on, as an admin set it on the uCRM catalogue screen (5.18.103's, byte for byte
#            in 5.18.104; Uganda since 4 Nov 2026), agents already see direct mode and the copy changes nothing of it; off
#            or never set, the forms quote as 5.18.103 does with it off; QC-N2 the installation product and the standard
#            quotations, defined and usable now; QC-N3 the applications by entry, quote_sale_entry web, app, web-direct or
#            none — F11's measure (§G.11); QC-N4 the web applications refused P1 with no quotation (quote_sale_entry web:
#            the KYC form under 5.18.102, or under 5.18.103 or 5.18.104 while the switch is off) — with the switch on each
#            is quoted in uCRM by hand (G-10), with it off Make the quotation applies once their items are linked; their
#            ids on
#            the sheet; QC-N5 the offered hardware with no active stock category of the same title (the stock deduction
#            matches by title, §G.7); QC-N6 the offered items public_price_exclude names — a hint, the forms never read
#            it (G-5); QC-N7 the plugin's own active plans by type, none of which direct mode draws. After the copy: QC-CA1
#            the same through the INSTALLED offered() and UcrmCatalogue on a fresh copy — in the deploy run equal to stage
#            A's ITEM BY ITEM (each item's verdict a keyed hash under the QL key, kept in a file of mode 0600 beside the
#            state file, never printed), unless the catalogue's settings changed since stage A (a note naming it); in an
#            --after-only run a note naming its direction; in either an unreadable catalogue, "other", the settings unread
#            or any request but a GET fails. QC-CA2 (stage V): the uCRM catalogue screen sends a visitor with no session to
#            the sign-in page, and the installed includes/post/post_sync.php guards its five actions — POST-only, inside
#            the gate, an admin, the account's fresh re-read and the own-page check before any write — read as text beside
#            the pin's. QC-CA3: Send Quotation and the lead quotes re-price picked lines inside QuotationService, as text
